# Fixed 2026-10-09, defect 530, lane b16-misc (class improvement).
# Symptom: n handles each ended in both branches of its own `if` cost the
# checker the square of n after defect 511's repair, 1.49, 3.74, 10.73 and
# 34.63 billion instructions at 500, 1,000, 2,000 and 4,000, and 107.28
# billion at 4,000 inside a loop.
# Cause: a path's first change copied what it shared with the base it went
# on from, and the groups were one array and the record of what changed a
# list and a map, so each branch and each join copied every local's group.
# The groups are a tree indexed by the local's number (`check/flow_groups`)
# and what changed is each group's stamp (`check/flow_log`): 1.10, 2.14,
# 4.21 and 8.36 billion, and 9.27 inside the loop, every verdict the same.
# This case: 300 handles each ended in both branches of its `if`, then the
# same inside a loop, where a read after the `if`s is refused for the first
# and the last; and beside them an end on one branch, read after it, and a
# handle opened and ended inside a branch, which are not.
extern "fixedbugs-530-three-hundred-ifs-each-ending-a-handle-copy-what-they-change.h"
    record Cell tag hh
    function f_open() -> Cell acquires f_close
    function f_close(x: Cell consumes)
    function f_peek(x: Cell) -> i64

